    // 交互式实验室：每个演示的说明和“模型说明与局限”
    demos: {
      rabi: {
        intro: T('一个被微波脉冲驱动的量子比特：从 |0⟩ 出发，看它在 Bloch 球上怎样转动，P(|1⟩) 怎样随时间振荡（Rabi 振荡），失谐和 T₁、T₂ 怎样让翻转变得不完全。',
          'A qubit driven by a microwave pulse: starting from |0⟩, watch how it rotates on the Bloch sphere, how P(|1⟩) oscillates in time (Rabi oscillation), and how detuning, T₁ and T₂ make the flip incomplete.'),
        notes: T('旋转坐标系、旋转波近似下的 Bloch 方程（第 02 节公式），四阶 Runge–Kutta 积分；Ω/2π 和 Δ/2π 以 MHz 为单位，时间以 μs 为单位。T₂ 被限制为不超过 2T₁。无衰减时与广义 Rabi 公式一致（误差小于 10⁻⁶）。没有包括 transmon 的第三能级（泄漏）、脉冲形状和读出误差。',
          'Bloch equations in the rotating frame under the rotating-wave approximation (formula in part 02), integrated with fourth-order Runge–Kutta; Ω/2π and Δ/2π in MHz, time in μs. T₂ is capped at 2T₁. Without damping it agrees with the generalised Rabi formula to better than 10⁻⁶. The transmon\'s third level (leakage), pulse shaping and readout error are not included.'),
      },
      budget: {
        intro: T('一台有 n 个比特的机器跑“砖墙式”随机电路：每层每个比特一个单比特门、⌊n/2⌋ 个两比特门，最后全部读出。调门误差，看整条电路的成功概率怎样随深度指数下降。',
          'A machine with n qubits runs a "brickwork" random circuit: each layer has one single-qubit gate per qubit and ⌊n/2⌋ two-qubit gates, followed by readout of every qubit. Adjust the gate errors and watch the whole circuit\'s success probability fall exponentially with depth.'),
        notes: T('数字误差模型（第 02 节公式）：假设每个门和读出的错误独立，任何一个错误都让整条电路失败。Sycamore 预设取 Arute 等人（2019）报告的同时运行时的平均误差：单比特门 0.16%、两比特门 0.62%、读出 3.8%；他们的电路门数与这里的砖墙电路不同，所以结果只在量级上可比。真实电路中有的错误不影响结果，有的错误会相干叠加；“方形电路”指标是本页为了直观自定义的，不是 IBM 的量子体积。',
          'The digital error model (formula in part 02): every gate and readout is assumed to fail independently, and any single error spoils the whole circuit. The Sycamore preset uses the average simultaneous errors reported by Arute et al. (2019): 0.16% for single-qubit gates, 0.62% for two-qubit gates and 3.8% for readout; their gate counts differ from this brickwork circuit, so results are comparable only in order of magnitude. In real circuits some errors do not affect the result and some add coherently; the "square circuit" figure is defined on this page for intuition and is not IBM\'s quantum volume.'),
      },
      qec: {
        intro: T('左边是重复码：精确的逻辑错误率与随机抽样的结果对照，看 p 低于还是高于 50% 时码距的作用相反。右边是表面码的计算器：给定物理错误率、逻辑比特数和运行轮数，估算需要的码距和物理比特数。',
          'On the left is the repetition code: the exact logical error rate against random sampling, showing that code distance helps below p = 50% and hurts above it. On the right is a surface-code calculator: given the physical error rate, the number of logical qubits and the number of rounds, it estimates the required distance and physical qubit count.'),
        notes: T('重复码只防比特翻转，假设错误独立、症状测量完美，所以阈值是 50%。表面码用 Fowler 等人（2012）的经验拟合 ε ≈ 0.03 (p/0.57%)^{(d+1)/2}（电路级噪声、最小权重匹配解码），总失败概率预算取 1%，物理比特数按旋转表面码 2d² − 1 计算，不含魔术态工厂、路由和解码硬件。不同的码、噪声模型和解码器会让结果相差数倍；它给的是量级，不是设计。',
          'The repetition code guards against bit flips only and assumes independent errors and perfect syndrome measurement, so its threshold is 50%. The surface code uses the empirical fit of Fowler et al. (2012), ε ≈ 0.03 (p/0.57%)^{(d+1)/2} (circuit-level noise, minimum-weight matching decoding), with a total failure budget of 1%; physical qubits are counted as 2d² − 1 for the rotated surface code, excluding magic-state factories, routing and decoding hardware. Different codes, noise models and decoders change the result several-fold; it gives an order of magnitude, not a design.'),
      },
    },

